# Example reverse-proxy config for maads.mirogeorgiev.eu.
# Copy this block into the box's real Caddyfile — this repo does not manage
# that file directly, since the domain is deployed manually (see
# webapp/README.md).
#
# Caddy gets free automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) with no config beyond this.
#
# One backend serves everything: the account app owns the origin and mounts the
# existing trace dashboard at /dashboard (webapp/backend/app.py). Splitting them
# across two ports with `handle` blocks does not work — both apps serve their
# own SPA at / and their own API at /api, so whichever block matched /api/*
# silently broke the other app's entire UI.

maads.mirogeorgiev.eu {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8766
}
